Assembler Version 11
====================
Assembled by: version 10 (both instgen and asm)

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
All features from version 10, plus additional instructions:

Syntax:
- Non-standard (custom) mnemonic syntax: LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, etc.
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Quoted strings with \n escape
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators on labels
- Relative branch (~label) syntax (also auto-detected via flags)
- Labels as 2-byte operands
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly
- Flag-based operand type detection
- Zero page addressing with plain hex values
- .include directive for including external files

Directives:
- .include filename - includes contents of another file at current position

Instruction set (expanded from v10):
- ADC#, ADCZ, AND#, ASLA
- BCC, BCS, BEQ, BITZ, BMI, BNE, BPL, BRK
- CLC, CMPZ, CMP#, CMP,Y, CPXZ, CPYZ, CPY#
- DECZ, DEX, DEY
- EORZ
- INCZ, INX, INY
- JMP, JSR
- LDA, LDX, LDY (absolute), LDA#, LDAZ(),Y, LDA,X, LDA,Y, LDAZ, LDAZ,X,
  LDXZ, LDYZ, LDX#, LDY#
- LSRA
- ORAZ
- PHA, PLA
- ROLZ, RTS
- SBC#, SBCZ, SEC
- STA, STAZ(),Y, STA,X, STA,Y, STAZ, STAZ,X, STXZ, STYZ
- TAX, TAY, TSX, TXA, TYA

Error handling: same as version 10 (errors 1-C)

New in this version (relative to version 10):
- New instructions: CPXZ, CPYZ, DEY, LDXZ, LDYZ, STXZ, STYZ
- Code modularization using .include: source split into multiple files
  (asm.asm, common.asm, environment.asm)
- Label hash table moved to $1F00 (from $4000)
- Heap placed after program code (HEAP label at end of source) instead of
  at a fixed address
- Hash tables reduced to 128 entries (CPY# $80 loop termination)
- calculate_hash preserves X register (TXA/PHA ... PLA/TAX)
- instgen.asm also uses .include for shared code (environment.asm, common.asm)
- Instruction hash table included from generated file (out/inst.asm.out)
  via .include rather than cat/prepend
- Environment I/O addresses documented in environment.asm with additional
  entry points: argc ($F01B), argv ($F01E), openout ($F021), write ($F024)

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
- Non-standard mnemonic syntax (LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, etc.)
- DATA pseudo-instruction
- Hex constants ($xx and $xxxx)
- Quoted strings with escape sequences
- Labels and label assignments
- PC setting (* = $2000 and * = $FFFC for vectors)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators
- Labels as absolute 2-byte operands
- Comments (;)
- BRK with inline error code and message
- .include directive (environment.asm, common.asm, out/inst.asm.out)
- Zero page variables addressed without < prefix
- Stack access via TSX and LDA,X for interrupt handler
- File I/O: open, close, read
- File stack operations (push/pop)

New syntax used in source (relative to version 10):
- .include directive (first version where the assembler's source uses .include)

Other source changes:
- Source split into: asm.asm (main), common.asm (shared code with instgen),
  environment.asm (I/O address definitions)
- instgen.asm also uses .include for common.asm and environment.asm
- Instruction hash table loaded via .include out/inst.asm.out (no longer
  prepended via cat)
- HEAP label defined at end of code rather than at a fixed address
